   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the town of Lansing, Tompkins county, to use certain lands conveyed thereto by the state for any purpose; and to repeal chapter 284 of the laws of 1993 relating to authorizing the town of Lansing, Tompkins county, to use certain lands conveyed thereto by the state for certain government purposes",
    "basePrintNo": "S5908",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5908-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Tompkins County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5908\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act in relation to authorizing the town of Lansing, Tompkins\ncounty, to use certain lands conveyed thereto by the state for any\npurpose; and to repeal chapter 284 of the laws of 1993 relating to\nauthorizing the town of Lansing, Tompkins county, to use certain lands\nconveyed thereto by the state for certain government purposes\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nThis legislation would lift current restrictions and authorize the\nTown of Lansing, in Tompkins County, to use certain land conveyed to\nthem by the state, for any purpose.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 authorizes the Town of Lansing to use certain lands conveyed\nto them by the state for any purposes whatsoever, including, without\nlimitation, the right and ability to sell or lease such land or\nportion thereof.\n\nSection 2 surrenders the right of reversion by the attorney general or\notherwise.\n\nSection 3 repeals chapter 284 of the laws of 1993 which authorized the\nTown of Lansing to use certain lands conveyed to them by the state for\ngovernment purposes.\n\nSection 4 contains the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nCurrently, the deed from the State of New York restricts the use of\nthis land for parkland or recreational use, and limits its other\npotential allowable purposes to those set for in Public Lands Law,\nSection 34. Legislative approval will facilitate the Town's plans to\ndevelop a proposed Town Center, which would provide an opportunity to\nbring light commercial development into the community. While a portion\nof the land would be retained for recreational purposes.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
