    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Tompkins County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5908A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act authorizing the commissioner of general services to sell\ncertain lands in the town of Lansing\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nAuthorizes the commissioner of general services to sell and convey\ncertain state lands in the town of Lansing consisting of the former\nstate department of social services training school for fair market\nvalue in return for unrestricted title.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSections 1-5 authorize the commissioner of general services to sell\nand convey unrestricted title for state lands to the town of Lansing\nin the county of Tompkins for fair market value for the property.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe land in question in this act was transferred to the town of\nLansing from the state in 1993 for use for recreational and community\ncenter purposes. With the continued development of the Lansing area,\nthe town has expressed the desire to consolidate town public and\nprivate activities in the area in and around this plot through a\nmaster plan, thereby preserving open and agricultural space further\nout of town. In order to do so, the reversion of title based on the\nland having a public purpose must be removed. To be consistent with\nstate policy, the town will have to pay the fair market value of the\nland to remove such restrictions on its purpose, as well as to\ntransfer or sell the land for any private use.\n\n HISTORY :\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nUndetermined at this time.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
